WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.333
AI is about to do the ordering. A fridge that reorders. A doctor at a distance.

2
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:11.167
But we do not live in the virtual world. The body has not changed in tens of thousands of years.

3
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:16.167
Food, water and medicine have to physically arrive. So more things will move.

4
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.167
Shipping is solved. Receiving is where it jams.

5
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:27.833
Japan hands parcels over in person. If you are out, it goes back — 400 million times a year.

6
00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:33.667
There are fewer drivers every year, and a van with no driver still comes back a second time.

7
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.500
America leaves it at the door. It gets taken, and everyone can see what you bought.

8
00:00:39.833 --> 00:00:45.333
And a robot that opens your front door? Overpower the robot, and you are inside the house.

9
00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:49.500
So delete the idea that you have to be home.

10
00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:56.167
A store on your way. Your office. A neighbour with a code that expires. Switched from your phone.

11
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:02.833
Drop a pin on any street, like parking a shared bike. Share your location, and it comes to you.

12
00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:07.833
Delivery OS. Packages adapt to people.
